
j2nb

Notes:
- Standalone devices and Virtual Chassis
- Junos only (junos-pyez)
- Can be run by Cron to keep Netbox in sync with the real world
- Need all the devices already existing in Netbox
- Need the VCs already configured in Netbox (FQDN as "domain" field)
- Supports VLANs
- Supports VC links
- Not tested on pfw
- Supports VRRP

Need to fix:
- Doesn't support interfaces with the same name on multiple VC members (that's also poorly implemented in Netbox)
Easy fix is to have FPC specific names (eg. em0-1, vcp-3/0/24)

To implement:
- Cross devices links (needed? they don't all have LLDP)
- SRX NAT IPs (might be easier to do it manually as they don't change often)
- L3 VLAN interfaces
- General fine tuning

How to use:
- Rename config.yml.example to config.yml (and configure it)
- Setup venv
- Install python requirements
- run with `python3 j2nb.py` (--dryrun optional)
